{"id": "EUVD-2026-81991", "enisaUuid": "31a126f4-d421-3fd8-af7e-3433aa6b1d55", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: logitech-hidpp: Fix FF device cleanup on init failure\n\nhidpp_ff_init() creates the input force-feedback device with\ninput_ff_create(), then allocates the HID++ FF private data,\neffect ID array, and workqueue.\n\nIf any of those allocations fail after input_ff_create() succeeds,\nthe function returns an error without destroying the FF device.\nAdd an unwind path that frees the private allocations made by\nhidpp_ff_init() and calls input_ff_destroy() for failures after\ninput_ff_create() succeeds.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/360a49fc53acdfe2dbb80c23cfa606ed7e13a85d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bb216586a3cb4ce327511a7c0445fa88e85b3cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fd9c8112907c14efefe6a90d20b774737052db3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13378c9ac0a1bcdf49ba158e4199594aafb589cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd5be4d9ce2dfc4d4a4527ef7d31d21a78e3cdac"], "aliases": ["GHSA-659p-736p-fqhx", "CVE-2026-90330"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07fbc2b8-ee1f-31f0-b712-71c3f06b5d44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff21a635dd1a9c6ca378847160897649cdbbfae4 <13378c9ac0a1bcdf49ba158e4199594aafb589cd"}, {"id": "1825db55-b8f8-3ef7-abc5-25cd490f0741", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.6"}, {"id": "21d75092-3dfb-3d90-89c3-ca33ba556ef2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2b28eaba-571b-3e27-9570-d3a3d31601b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3fdd45fc-6431-3ff3-8d2c-2b5516e39cfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff21a635dd1a9c6ca378847160897649cdbbfae4 <360a49fc53acdfe2dbb80c23cfa606ed7e13a85d"}, {"id": "455c05ba-b03c-3afb-8cc7-412a7e06313b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "69b5f1e2-1a9d-38eb-b5c9-c2b48bc2b979", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff21a635dd1a9c6ca378847160897649cdbbfae4 <6bb216586a3cb4ce327511a7c0445fa88e85b3cb"}, {"id": "791dddf3-c462-3307-9e96-dbf8a773c3f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "8ba74247-0a32-33a2-a1c5-9095c250f975", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "9116da1b-fdc8-3308-8f5a-d69084cef96b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "928509f6-50b3-3f6f-b8b9-f63e75f60f91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff21a635dd1a9c6ca378847160897649cdbbfae4 <2fd9c8112907c14efefe6a90d20b774737052db3"}, {"id": "be78b139-eee3-3ad1-b592-50fed1ae9565", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff21a635dd1a9c6ca378847160897649cdbbfae4 <dd5be4d9ce2dfc4d4a4527ef7d31d21a78e3cdac"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4a16d75b-5aeb-32c6-92ab-8a56d3103b65", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}